# Migration plan (Lab → product)

The Design Lab is frozen as the visual reference. Migrate in this order — do not
skip lots; do not start Accueil before Shell and Match.

## Lot 0 — Final arbitrations ✅

- Angle: **12°**
- Width: fluid 100% with lateral gutters (no centered max-width column)
- Match Hero, numeric roles, icon rules, surface hierarchy — validated in Lab V2

## Lot 1 — Foundations

Tokens, typography, brand, Wordmark, PlayUpMark, live (distinct from success),
numeric roles, icons. Port Lab patterns into `design-system/`.

## Lot 2 — Shell

Rail + wordmark + competition context + navigation. First shared surface for all routes.

## Lot 3 — Match

Match Hero → score → live → actions → events. The sport-identity showcase.

## Lot 4 — Cockpit

State → hero number → next action → À traiter.

## Lot 5 — Classements / Calendrier

Numeric grammar at full intensity (zones, trends, matchdays).

## Lot 6 — Accueil

Brand entry point — after the operational grammar is proven.

## Lot 7 — Legacy purge

Anything that does not match the Design Lab is suspect. Remove `index.css` legacy
palette, pills, ghost tokens, duplicated components.

## Rule during migration

Each lot must pass the acceptance test: **could this have been designed in the Lab?**
If not, extend the Lab first (gap only — no new artistic direction).
